# ── wisli PaddleOCR server (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# When set, the Scan tab sends images to this server (PaddleOCR PP-StructureV3)
# instead of running Tesseract.js in the browser. Leave blank to use the
# offline Tesseract fallback.
#
# The server is the FastAPI app in the wisli repo (tools/ocr_server). Run it on
# a machine with PaddleOCR, expose it over HTTPS (e.g. Cloudflare Tunnel), then
# put that public URL here. MUST be https:// (the deployed app is https, so an
# http:// OCR URL is blocked as mixed content).
#
# Local dev:   copy this file to ".env" and fill in.
# Vercel:      add these as Project → Settings → Environment Variables, then redeploy.
VITE_OCR_SERVER_URL=
# Only needed if the server sets OCR_API_KEY. NOTE: a value here ships in the
# public client bundle — fine for an ephemeral tunnel, not a long-lived secret.
VITE_OCR_SERVER_API_KEY=
